### Olga — signed in, a member of nothing — names Acme. A tenant the person does not belong to refuses the whole
### principal: never a quieter, tenantless caller who might still read something.
# @name OlgaNamesAcme
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [401]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=reference.asc
Authorization: Bearer {{OlgaAccess}}
X-Alvo-Tenant: {{AcmeId}}

### Olga names no tenant: she acts in none, and a scoped entity answers the tenant guard
# @name OlgaNamesNothing
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=reference.asc
Authorization: Bearer {{OlgaAccess}}

### The control: the same request by Acme's dispatcher
# @name DanaNamesAcme
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=reference.asc
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
X-Alvo-Tenant: {{AcmeId}}

### A tenantless person still reads global data: `regions.list` asks only that the caller is authenticated
# @name OlgaReadsRegions
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions?code=eq.{{RegionCode}}
Authorization: Bearer {{OlgaAccess}}
